  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nLatest models show the upper low exiting our CWA Monday before \ntropical moisture can get into the low's circulation, which \nmeans our CWA should miss out on that moisture. But a weak upper\ntrough from the north Pacific will still produce a slight \nchance of late-day showers Wednesday and Thursday. Temperatures \non those days will be slightly above normal, with Friday likely\neven a little warmer. A cold front and stronger upper trough \nshould bring windy, cooler weather Friday night and Saturday, \nwith a better chance of showers.",
